  <item>
    <title>Marion County: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/marion-county-fl</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-marion-county-fl</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Planning and Zoning Commission voted unanimously to recommend a 12-month moratorium on new data centers, cryptocurrency mining and related facilities after a packed public hearing. Goes to the Board of County Commissioners for a second public hearing on Sept 15, 2026; not adopted yet. Commissioners had earlier directed staff to prepare a 12-month pause rather than the six months first suggested.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Orange County: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/orange-county-fl</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-orange-county-fl</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Vice Mayor Kelly Martinez Semrad asked the county commission to consider a moratorium of at least one year on new AI data center applications; the board takes it up Sept 15, 2026. County land development code has no data center definition, so the use is implicitly allowed in industrial districts. Proposal calls for study of water, energy capacity, zoning and community character.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Clay County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/clay-county-fl</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-clay-county-fl</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Board of County Commissioners voted 4-1 to adopt a one-year moratorium on data center rezoning, permits, and site plans; Commissioner Compere sole no vote; staff to research potential impacts on water and infrastructure</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Nassau County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/nassau-county-fl</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-nassau-county-fl</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Board of County Commissioners adopted Ordinance 2026-044, a 12-month moratorium on acceptance, review, or approval of applications for development permits, rezoning, or site plans for data centers, data processing, data mining, or cryptocurrency mining; county established a Fact-Finding Committee on Data Center Development; prompted by NextNRG&#x27;s 1,600-acre lease option near Jacksonville International Airport</description>
  </item>
